         I1.3.1 The upper and lower ice waterlines upon which the design of the ship has been based
         is to be indicated in the Certificate of Classification. The upper ice waterline (UIWL) is to be
         defined by the maximum draughts fore, amidships and aft. The lower ice waterline (LIWL) is
         to be defined by the minimum draughts fore, amidships and aft.

         I1.3.2 The lower ice waterline is to be determined with due regard to the ship’s ice-going
         capability in the ballast loading conditions. The propeller is to be fully submerged at the lower
         ice waterline.




